#N canvas 40 40 760 780 12;
#X text 20 20 Cut It -- entry point on the Organelle. mother.pd loads this file by name. Keep it thin: it instantiates u_root and nothing else., f 52;
#X obj 20 120 u_root 17 1 /sdcard/cut-it-state 33 49;
#X text 20 250 The 17 is the Pd channel the nanoKONTROL's own channel 1 lands on and the 1 is the Launchpad's. They are Pd INPUT SLOTS 2 and 1 here \, per /root/.pdsettings \, and slot n gets channels (n-1)*16+1 upward. Set the Mac's MIDI inputs to the same order -- Launchpad first \, nano second -- and main-dev.pd can pass the same two numbers \, which is the point of doing it that way round. The third argument is u_state's DATA DIRECTORY \, and it is the one thing the two entry points genuinely CANNOT share: there is no /sdcard on a Mac. /sdcard survives deploy.sh \, deploy.sh --clean and a power cycle \, which the patch folder does not -- so the instrument's data is never at the mercy of a code push. THE FOURTH AND FIFTH ARE THE OUTPUT DEVICES -- 33 is the SP-404's own channel 1 (slot 3) and 49 is the Volca's (slot 4 \, the USB Uno). ⚠️ Pd 0.49 does NOT warn about a missing or extra creation argument \, and POSITIONAL ARGS CANNOT BE SKIPPED \, so 33 is passed here even though m_404 does not exist yet -- leaving it out would silently make the Volca's channel arrive as arg 4., f 52;
#X text 20 170 The Mac entry point is main-dev.pd \, which adds u_mother-stub. It ships in this folder and the device never loads it., f 52;
